            <ArticleTitle>Successful crossing of a severe spasm of the brachial artery using a telescopic approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of severe brachial artery spasm resistant to vasodilator treatment. A multi-purpose 110 cm diagnostic catheter was used as an inner dilator. This allowed easy negotiation of a guiding catheter through the tortuous segment and successful completion of the angioplasty procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
